>> title: Nikumiso
>> category: Toppings & Pickles
>> tags: japanese, pork, miso, make ahead, condiment, pantry
>> counters: Japanese Home Cooking
>> aka: 肉味噌, nikumiso, nikumiso, にくみそ, 肉みそ, miso pork, minced pork in miso, meat miso
>> pairs-with: gohan, tamagoyaki
>> servings: 8
>> time: 25 min
>> slack: forgiving — a high flame once the miso is in browns it and leaves a burnt-bitter edge that cannot be cooked back out

>> step: fry 1 min, before the garlic colours
Fry @ginger{1%Tbs}(grated), @garlic{1%clove}(grated) and @scallions{3}(white parts, chopped fine) in @toasted sesame oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) in a #frying pan{} ~fry{1%min}, until it smells and before the garlic takes any colour.

>> step: brown 6 min, until it catches
Brown @ground pork{12%oz}(340 g) in @&(~1)aromatics{} ~fry{6%min}, breaking it up as it goes, until the water it gives off has boiled away and the meat starts to catch on the pan.

>> step: cook down 8 min to a furrow
Stir @red miso{1/4%cup}(70 g), @sake{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @mirin{2%Tbs}(30 mL) and @sugar{1%Tbs} into @&(~1)pork{} and ~cook{8%min} over the lowest flame, stirring, until a spoon dragged through the middle leaves a furrow that stays open for a second.
